    "title": "Server room (12 racks): 2N UPS, maintenance bypass, redundant PDUs A/B", "project": "EX-23",
    "client": "Example Office Campus, IT", "author": "uniwire examples", "lang": "en",
    "notes": [
      "Demonstrates: two independent UPS paths (2N), external maintenance bypass switch fed by a 'transfer' link, key interlock recorded with 'locks' and 'interlocks', PDUs (board kind 'pdu'), EPO 'trip' link to the incomer shunt trip",
      "Each UPS has its own VRLA battery cabinet (2 strings, 9.6 kWh); EPO also stops both UPS via dry contact",
      "Every rack has dual-corded equipment fed from PDU-A and PDU-B (same rack number)",
      "Key interlock: maintenance bypass -QA4/-QB4 can be switched only with key KA/KB released by -QA2/-QB2 open"
    ]
  },
  "installation": {
    "earthing": "TN-S", "system": "3P+N", "un_V": 400, "uln_V": 230, "f_Hz": 50, "ik3_kA": 15,
